; print must write back the {{total}} lot price each posting wrote.  The
; total is divided into a per-unit price, rounded when the division does
; not terminate, and that per-unit lot is shared by every posting of the
; same lot, however each one wrote its price.  So print takes the total,
; and whether there was one, from the posting, never from the shared lot:
; rebuilding it from the rounded per-unit price printed {{$99.99999999}}
; for {{$100.00}}, and the shared lot made a later posting print an
; earlier posting's form ({{...}} or {...}).

